    </h3>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-section-body field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p><span><strong>Motorboat</strong> means any watercraft 65 feet in length or less that is subject to the ORS 830.005 regulations set out herein. Motorboat classification OAR 250-10-140.&nbsp; All motorboats are classified according to their length, as follows:</span></p><ol class="code-list"><li><strong>A.&nbsp; </strong>Motorboats under 16’ in length - Class “A”</li><li><strong>B.&nbsp; </strong>Motorboats 16’ in length, but less than 26’ -Class “1”</li><li><strong>C.&nbsp; </strong>Motorboats 26’ in length, but less than 40’ - Class “2”</li><li><strong>D.&nbsp; </strong>Motorboats 40’ in length, but less than 65’ - Class “3”</li></ol></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
